WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.221
Calculated column or measure?

2
00:00:02.221 --> 00:00:06.128
It is the most common question new Power BI users ask.

3
00:00:06.128 --> 00:00:11.101
In this lesson, you will learn how each one behaves in a visual, how

4
00:00:11.101 --> 00:00:15.719
to change the way a column is summarized, and when to use which.

5
00:00:15.719 --> 00:00:17.140
Let's clear it up!

6
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:24.926
In Table view, here is our calculated column, Total Amount, at the end of the Shipments table.

7
00:00:24.926 --> 00:00:28.760
It has a value on every row, stored in the table.

8
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:58.860
On the report, I add a table visual, and drag in Amount, Boxes, and Total Amount.

9
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:21.043
Power BI adds up the columns automatically.

10
00:01:21.043 --> 00:01:27.220
The visual shows the sum of Total Amount, the sum of Amount, and the sum of Boxes.

11
00:01:53.500 --> 00:01:58.913
Right click a field in the Columns box to change how it is summarized:

12
00:01:58.913 --> 00:02:01.620
Sum, Average, Minimum, Maximum, Count, and more.

13
00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:12.741
Here I choose Average for Amount and Minimum for another field.

14
00:02:12.741 --> 00:02:15.440
Same column, different summary, in one click.

15
00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:25.450
So what is the difference?

16
00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:29.740
A calculated column is computed once, for each row, and stored.

17
00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:33.250
It is great for labels, groups, and row-level math.

18
00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:37.540
A measure is calculated on the fly, for whatever is selected.

19
00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:40.660
It is best for totals, averages, and ratios.

20
00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:59.740
Back in Table view, the Total Amount column formula is Amount times Boxes, row by row.

21
00:03:10.500 --> 00:03:11.047
Simple rule:

22
00:03:11.047 --> 00:03:13.507
if you need it per row, use a column.

23
00:03:13.507 --> 00:03:17.060
If you need it as a summary, use a measure. You've got it!

